  "intended_use": "Research and development use inside the Velos/SPARK platform: optional refinement of EPRY reconstructions of the in-house LED-array microscope (633 nm, 4x/0.10, 15x15 LEDs at 3 mm, about 55-60 mm below the sample) acquired with a reduced LED set (all LEDs inside 1.1 x NA plus 30-50 % of the dark-field LEDs), followed by the hybrid physics polish. The physics result is always kept and returned alongside.",
  "limitations": [
    "Fine-tuned on ONE field of view per specimen type (blood smear; leaf section), left 65 % of a 645 um patch, five acquisitions; tested on the right 35 %, on unseen LED draws and on sensor regions never used for training. Other specimens, objectives, wavelengths or LED geometries are out of distribution.",
    "Validated for the BLOOD SMEAR in the hybrid mode (model + 5 EPRY passes): closer to the full-LED reconstruction and slightly lower prediction error on the LEDs not used. The model output alone removes reduced-LED artefacts but does not predict unmeasured LED images better: use it for viewing, not for quantitative values. NOT validated for the leaf section (its output contradicts the measured images; prediction error +34 to +105 %).",
    "Outputs are estimates, not measurements: use the data-consistency check (residual on the LEDs used and prediction error on LEDs not used) and prefer the physics or hybrid result when it disagrees.",
    "References are full-LED EPRY reconstructions, not ground truth; their own repeatability is reported in the evaluation summary."
  ],
